# Vercel production: push GitHub, not only origin

**Production source of truth:** [goropojixoj12-oss/lox-voice](https://github.com/goropojixoj12-oss/lox-voice) on GitHub (`github` remote), branch `main`. Vercel production deploys from that repo.

**`origin`** is the Cursor/cloud mirror (`origin.cursor.com`). Pushing only `origin` does **not** update Vercel.

## After ANY commit on this project

1. Run **`./scripts/push-production.sh`** (preferred), or equivalently:
   - `git push -u github main` (required)
   - `git push -u origin main` if the `origin` remote exists
2. Confirm **`git push` to `github` succeeded** (exit code 0, no errors).
3. Do **not** mark the task complete, tell the user work is shipped, or assume Vercel updated until `github/main` has the commit.

## Feature branches

When work lands on `main` (merge or direct commit on `main`), still push **`github main`**. For long-lived feature branches, push the branch to both remotes if needed, but **production verification is always `github/main`.**

## If push fails

Fix auth/network/permissions, retry until `github` push succeeds. Report the blocker to the user if you cannot resolve it.

**Do not** use GitHub MCP (`create_or_update_file`, `push_files`) as a workaround for `package-lock.json` or other large files — see `no-github-mcp-for-lockfile.mdc`.
